## 2. Network / archive serialization

### Problem the split solves (both trees — convergent)

| Mechanism | Evidence |
|-----------|----------|
| **Compile/link hygiene** — move heavy `Archive::get/put` specializations out of public headers into `.cpp` | New: `AuctionQueryArchive.cpp`, `ClientCentralMessagesArchive.cpp`, `AIDebuggingMessagesArchiveTypes.h`, etc. (identical file set in both diffs vs `949451032`) |
| **Type isolation** — message structs separated from archive logic | e.g. `AuctionQueryTypes.h:18-34` struct fields explicitly `int32`/`int64` |
| **Duplicate `uint64` symbols** — B documents moving overloads into `Archive.h` | `NetworkIdArchive.cpp:19-24` (B): “removed to avoid duplicate-symbol clash”; A keeps impl in `NetworkIdArchive.cpp:21-45` |
| **`PackedArchive.{h,cpp}`** | Both trees: thin `PackedTransform` adapter only (`PackedArchive.cpp:20-30`) — **not** the network-message split |

Base `949451032` had **no** `include/public/.../AuctionQueryArchive.h`; both forks introduced the same split pattern independently.

### Wire-format comparison

| Layer | On-wire contract | Repo A | Repo B | Protocol risk |
|-------|------------------|--------|--------|---------------|
| Generic `AutoDeltaMap` pack/unpack | 4-byte counts | `AutoDeltaMap.h:362-363,537-538` `uint32_t` | `AutoDeltaMap.h` `static_cast<uint32_t>` on put; unpack `uint32_t commandCount` | **Low — aligned** |
| `Archive.h` `std::map` | 4-byte count | `uint32_t` | `int` (4-byte overload) | **Low** |
| **`AutoDeltaPackedMap` specializations** (Unicode / NetworkId string maps) | **4-byte** counts on 32-bit server | **`size_t` → on x64 binds `uint64` 8-byte get/put** (`UnicodeAutoDeltaPackedMap.cpp:60-64`, `NetworkIdAutoDeltaPackedMap.cpp:54-58`) | **`int32_t` explicit** (`UnicodeAutoDeltaPackedMap.cpp:25-26,60-64`) per `e0d46921e` | **HIGH for A on x64** — pack/unpack misaligns stream by 4 bytes per map delta |
| `NetworkId` / `int64` payloads | 8-byte | Both: 8-byte via `NetworkIdArchive` | Same | **Low** |
| B-only defensive reads | — | — | `Archive.h` `std::string`/`ByteStream` get throws `ReadException` if `size > remaining` | No wire change; hardens malformed packets |

**Repo A gap to close:** apply B’s `e0d46921e` pattern to `UnicodeAutoDeltaPackedMap.cpp`, `NetworkIdAutoDeltaPackedMap.cpp`, `AutoDeltaNetworkIdPackedMap.h` (and verify no other `size_t` count getters bind the 8-byte overload on x64).

